1002→Table~\ref{tab:walltime} summarizes total simulation times. The toggle switch achieves the largest speedup at 9.8$\times$ (364~s reduced to 37~s), benefiting from slower reaction timescales and compact state space geometry. The Oregonator and ROBER systems achieve 3.9$\times$ and 3.5$\times$ speedups respectively (4000~s $\to$ 1093~s and 10421~s $\to$ 3015~s). The consistent performance gains across diverse system types demonstrate that forward enumeration is the preferred construction method.
